hadiths[18]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1113","Narrated Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): He (peace be upon him) said: ""When the believers will be saved from the Hellfire, they will be stopped on a bridge between Paradise and Hell. Then they will settle the injustices that occurred between them in the world, until when they are purified and cleansed, they will be permitted to enter Paradise. By Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad (peace be upon him), each person will recognize his home in Paradise better than he recognized his home in this world."""
"1114","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Indeed, Allah will bring the believer close and will screen him and conceal him, and will say, 'Do you know such-and-such sin? Do you know such-and-such sin?' He will say, 'Yes, O Lord!' until Allah will make him confess all his sins, and he will think in his heart that he is ruined. Then Allah will say, 'I concealed them for you in the world, and today I forgive you for them.' Then he will be given the record of his good deeds. But as for the disbelievers and hypocrites, the witnesses will say (publicly) regarding them, 'These are the ones who lied against their Lord.' Behold! The curse of Allah is upon the wrongdoers."""
"1115","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim, so he should neither oppress him nor disgrace him. Whoever is engaged in fulfilling the need of his brother, Allah Almighty fulfills his need, and whoever removes a calamity from a Muslim, Allah Almighty will remove one of his calamities from the calamities of the Day of Resurrection. And whoever conceals the fault of a Muslim, Allah Almighty will conceal his fault on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"1116","Narrated Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Help your brother, whether he is an oppressor or is oppressed."" The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) said, ""O Messenger of Allah! We understand how to help the oppressed, but how should we help the oppressor?"" He (peace be upon him) said: ""By holding his hand."" (i.e., by preventing him from committing oppression)."
"1117","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, darknesses will be imposed upon the oppressor due to his oppression."""
"1118","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever has wronged his brother concerning his honor or anything else, he should seek his forgiveness today, before there will be neither dinar nor dirham (i.e., before the Day of Resurrection). If he has any good deeds, they will be taken from him in proportion to his wrongdoing, and if he has no good deeds, the sins of the wronged person will be loaded onto him."" (We seek refuge with Allah from that.)"
"1119","Sayyiduna Saeed bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever seizes even a little land of someone unjustly, on the Day of Resurrection, the seven layers of that land will be made into a collar and placed around the neck of that (oppressor)."""
"1120","Narrated Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever wrongfully takes a piece of land belonging to someone else, he will be made to sink down through the seven earths on the Day of Resurrection."""
"1121","`Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) passed by a people who were eating dates, so he said that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade eating two dates together at once, unless you seek permission from your brother (who is eating with you).`"
"1122","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The most disliked person to Allah Almighty is the one who is extremely quarrelsome."""
"1123","Umm al-Mu'mineen Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) heard the sound of a dispute at the door of his chamber, so he (peace be upon him) came out (the case was presented). Then he (peace be upon him) said: ""I am also a human being (I do not know the unseen). People who have disputes come to me for judgment, so perhaps one of you is more eloquent in presenting his case than the other, so I think that he has spoken the truth, and I give a decision in his favor because of this. So if I (unknowingly) give someone the right of another Muslim, then (he should understand that) it is a piece of Hellfire; now he may take it or leave it."""
"1124","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We asked the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) that when you send us out, sometimes we come to people who do not offer us hospitality. What do you say about this? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you go to such people and they provide you with what is due to a guest, then accept it. And if they do not do so, then take your right of hospitality from them."""
"1125","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No neighbor should prevent his neighbor from fixing pegs in his wall."" So Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: ""What is the matter that I find you people turning away from this hadith? By Allah! I will surely narrate this hadith before you."""
"1126","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Avoid sitting in the pathways."" The people said, ""We are compelled (to do so) because these are our sitting places where we converse with each other."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Alright! If you must sit there, then give the pathway its due right."" The people asked, ""What is the right of the pathway?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Lowering the gaze (from looking at those whom it is not permissible to look at), refraining from causing harm, returning greetings, enjoining good, and forbidding evil."""
"1127","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) had decided to leave seven cubits when people disputed over a pathway."
"1128","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Yazid Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade looting and mutilation."
"1129","Narrated Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-As (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever is killed while protecting his wealth is a martyr."""
"1130","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with one of his wives (Mother of the Believers Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her) when another Mother of the Believers (Safiyyah, may Allah be pleased with her, or Hafsah, may Allah be pleased with her) sent a bowl with some food through a servant. The wife with whom the Prophet (peace be upon him) was, struck the servant's hand and broke the bowl. The Prophet (peace be upon him) joined the pieces together and put the food in it and said: ""Eat."" And the Prophet (peace be upon him) kept the servant and the bowl until everyone had finished eating, then he (peace be upon him) gave a sound bowl and kept the broken one."
